    "V13-SCORER-ENDOGENEITY: the provenance score's trust signal is execution-grounded agreement of the shipped certificate with frozen historical truth labels; it is endogenous to the certificate (it measures whether our instruments can verify this origin's history), not an exogenous reputation source. In this construction the inferred allowlist coincides with the correct fiat list {O1,O2,O3,O4}; the demonstrated value of measuring is robustness to an OVER-PERMISSIVE fiat allowlist (C-FIAT-OVERTRUST FA=3 vs measured T FA=0), NOT that measurement beats a correct fiat list. A real deployment would need an independent provenance signal; this packet does not supply one.",
    "Zero-false-accept is within-envelope by frozen construction (WITHIN_ENVELOPE excludes BOUNDARY B11). B11 is the deliberately reachable closed-world/probe-reachability boundary that DOES fire (T FA=3), so the guarantee is conditional and not general.",
    "Cost figures are loopback HTTP counts and candidate counts only; real-world provenance/allowlist administration, ledger maintenance and negative-bank acquisition costs were not measured (model_calls=0, model_tokens=0 by construction).",
    "M-T-COVERAGE is compared same-bank against M-B-SHIPPED-COVERAGE (20/44=0.4545); the absolute 0.6750 constant is the parent's historical shipped-coverage anchor on the frozen seven-family bank, retained only as a floor anchor."
  ],
